Across the mall, UDF personnel watched civilians acquire tickets to an entertainment being staged inside the perimeter they themselves had been unable to enter.\
A corporal asked whether he could have one.\
His lieutenant told him no.\
The corporal accepted a T-shirt instead.\
Within twelve minutes, the promoters had developed a system. Locals got tickets. Elvi got tickets. Anyone claiming to know Alexander got tickets. Anyone claiming to know Eloise got better tickets. Important-looking people received cream envelopes embossed with the 
\f2\i Candid Criminal
\f1\i0  wheel and were assured Mr Shakti would be delighted if they attended.\
Several immediately became important-looking.\
The minibus continued spruiking after Alexander\'92s convoy had disappeared towards Sublime Point.\
By lunchtime, half the village had been invited to watch somebody die.\
The other half was furious they hadn\'92t been asked.\
